 INSERT INTO test_diary VALUES(13,'BOB-093','2026-08-21T21:21:34Z','AI-agent','SKIP','Bound-calibration debt recorded on the ledger rather than left as a doc sentence (§11.4.197), at the independent reviewer''s explicit request. The re_threads 4096-byte and gap 512-byte bounds are calibrated against SYNTHETIC fixtures whose largest row is 315 B. Against a reviewer-reconstructed realistic 1,415-byte row (242-char Cyrillic title, full 10-column markup) the two tightest margins are 2.9x and 2.6x — not the 13x/8x the doc originally claimed, which were fixture-relative.','The decision NOT to raise the bounds is ENDORSED by the reviewer, with an argument worth preserving: raising a bound is not free safety, because it linearly raises the ADVERSARIAL budget the bound exists to cap (measured: b=8192 gives a 3.77s worst case, ~2.6x the current). Raising on a hypothesised row shape with zero observed instances would trade a MEASURED DoS budget for an UNMEASURED truncation risk — a §11.4.6 guess in the opposite direction. With the new divergence telemetry emitting exact counts, keep-and-calibrate-from-observation is the §11.4.101 reversible-safe default. Blocked, not deferred by choice: no real rutracker page can be obtained — see BOB-172, where the search endpoint returns 403 with Cloudflare challenge markers and zero login markers, independently re-confirmed by the reviewer with cookie-bearing curl. That also makes this item''s own sub-step 4 (time a large page under 2s) unmeetable until BOB-172 resolves.','No bound changed. Debt is now on the ledger and linked to its blocker rather than living only in docs/qa/BOB-093/redos_timing.md, so it cannot quietly evaporate (§11.4.197).',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'regex_bound_calibration','2026-08-21 21:21:34');
 INSERT INTO test_diary VALUES(14,'BOB-161','2026-08-21T21:21:48Z','AI-agent','SKIP','Measured the CM-NO-FAIL-OPEN-SKIP claim. The name resolves in exactly two places: constitution/scripts/gates/gate_ledger_prev_names.txt:347 (the §11.4.227(A) previously-known-gate-names registry) and three sites in tests/e2e/test_live_stack_evidence.py — all three of which are COMMENTS. Per §11.4.227(A) prose carriers never count as implementation, so the gate NAME is genuinely unimplemented. Control needle: the same query resolves CM-CLOSURE-SEAM-BINDS to two EXECUTABLE sites (scripts/pre_build_verification.sh and scripts/pre_build/check_cm_closure_seam_binds.sh), so the carrier-only result is a real distinction and not a blind query.','The distinction that matters, and which the item as filed does not draw: the gate NAME is unimplemented, but the BEHAVIOUR is guarded. tests/e2e/test_live_stack_evidence.py:252-262 really does assert it — on a non-authenticated non-success result it calls _auth_failure_is_definitive() and pytest.fail()s on a definitive class, with the comment recording that the OLD code skipped unconditionally and asserted ''transient outage'' as fact, turning rejected credentials (upstream_http_403) and a broken container (plugin_env_missing) into PASS-counting SKIPs. So this is a ledger/naming gap, not a coverage hole. Conflating the two would be wrong in either direction: reporting it as unguarded overstates the risk, and closing it because the behaviour is tested would leave the §11.4.227(A) ledger permanently inaccurate.','No change. Item re-scoped by measurement: the fix is to either implement a named gate asserting the fail-open invariant, or register an explicit deferral citing test_live_stack_evidence.py as the behavioural cover — §11.4.227(A) requires one or the other, and ''the behaviour is tested somewhere'' is not by itself a valid ledger entry.',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'gate_ledger','2026-08-21 21:21:48');
 INSERT INTO test_diary VALUES(15,'BOB-174','2026-08-22T10:25:24Z','AI-agent','SKIP','The BOB-173 reviewer''s mutation R2 narrowed _save_hooks from `except Exception` to `except OSError` and SURVIVED all 17 tests. So the non-OSError arm of that handler is unpinned: the guard suite proves the I/O failure path is honest, but nothing pins the serialisation failure path. Failing scenario under the mutant: a caller hands _save_hooks a non-JSON-serialisable value; open("w") has ALREADY truncated hooks.json; json.dump raises TypeError, which escapes unlabelled; the endpoint''s `except HookPersistenceError` misses it, so a 500 arrives only via the global handler at api/__init__.py:186-189 — after the store has been left a truncated fragment.','Classified MINOR rather than IMPORTANT because the reviewer PROVED the path unreachable via the API today rather than assuming it (§11.4.194(2)): every persisted field is parsed-JSON body content, str(uuid4()), an isoformat string, a bool, or a ge/le-bounded int — none can carry a non-serialisable value. It becomes reachable the moment a future caller persists anything richer.','Filed here rather than against BOB-173 on the reviewer''s recommendation, because the truncated-fragment half is precisely this item''s chain: truncate -> _load_hooks swallows the corrupt file to [] -> the next save destroys the survivors. The three-line pin (`with pytest.raises(HookPersistenceError): _save_hooks([{"x": object()}])`) should land alongside the atomic-write fix, since together they close both the reporting and the integrity halves of the same failure. Also confirmed by the reviewer: theme_state.py:113-126 already carries the correct donor pattern (mkstemp + fsync + os.replace) — reuse it, do not re-invent (§11.4.28).',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'hook_persistence','2026-08-22 10:25:24');
+INSERT INTO test_diary VALUES(16,'BOB-097','2026-09-25T14:34:25Z','AI-agent','FAIL','Independently re-verified the crashed subagent''s 3 DDoS-coverage test files. 2/3 clean: test_auth_stress_chaos.py (7 tests, 1.71s, all PASS) and test_download_trigger_stress_chaos.py (8 tests, 1.65s, all PASS) -- both committed as genuine BOB-097 progress. 1/3 genuinely broken: test_sse_stream_stress_chaos.py::TestThemeStreamBurstIsRefusedNotServed::test_burst_of_stream_opens_is_refused_past_the_limit_with_no_5xx hangs indefinitely (reproduced 3x: original dispatch >13min, retry >13min, isolated re-run needed a hard ''timeout 20'' wrapper to terminate it at all). Root cause (traced via pytest-timeout --timeout-method=thread stack dump): the test opens ''with c.stream(...)'' against a starlette TestClient SSE endpoint with no client-side read timeout; the call blocks deep inside concurrent.futures.Future.result() -> threading.Condition.wait() -> waiter.acquire() while portal.call() invokes the FastAPI SSE handler in an anyio worker thread -- a genuine C-level lock acquire that pytest-timeout''s thread-based interrupt CANNOT break (the well-known Python limitation: a thread blocked in a C-level lock.acquire() is not interruptible by an injected exception). NOT committed. BOB-097 stays Queued/incomplete: the SSE stress-chaos coverage this item asks for still needs a correct implementation (bounded byte/event read count or an explicit httpx timeout= on the stream() call, plus investigating whether the app''s own SSE handler has a connection-limit-refusal path that never fires in test conditions).','This is exactly why crashed-subagent work is never trusted without independent re-verification -- one of the three files silently didn''t work at all, would have hung the CI/pre-build sweep indefinitely if committed and run automatically.','status unchanged',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'ddos_test_authoring','2026-09-25 14:34:25');
