an inferred from whatever the patch does. Candidates worth weighing: exempt the reopen path explicitly, require an override flag on `update` mirroring reopen''s, or leave the direction detective-only with the rationale recorded so the asymmetry is a decision rather than an oversight. (b) If a guard lands, it reuses `terminalStatuses()` — BOB-166 established one predicate source specifically so the two directions cannot drift. (c) Paired §1.1 mutation. (d) NEGATIVE CONTROL (§11.4.201(1)), and it is the sharp one here: the sanctioned reopen path MUST still work. A guard that breaks reopenCmd''s documented override is a false-positive refusal, and worse than the gap it closes, because it breaks a workflow operators are told to use.\u000a\u000aHONEST BOUNDARY. This is not a live data defect. Zero corpus instances, and the detective gate catches it at the next validate. It is filed so a scoped, deliberate omission stays visible as a tracked decision instead of living only in a code comment where the next reader will mistake it for an oversight (§11.4.197: a started thread reaches a documented terminal state, never quiet abandonment).\u000a\u000aPROVENANCE. Raised by the implementing agent of BOB-166 as a known asymmetry it deliberately did not close, independently verified and endorsed as an acceptable scope boundary by that item''s reviewer, on the condition that it become a tracked item rather than a comment. This is that item.\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 11:48:31','2026-09-25 11:48:31',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-223','Bug','Fixed (→ Fixed.md)','major','§11.4.18 script-documentation and §11.4.44 revision headers are ungated — and the perverse consequence is that WRITING the mandated companion doc is what breaks the build',unistr('WHAT, both conductor-verified with control needles: CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC occurrences in scripts/pre_build_verification.sh = 0 (control needle CM-MARKDOWN-EXPORT-SYNC = 6, so the instrument sees). §11.4.44 revision-header enforcement likewise 0 hits (control needle 3). Neither §11.4.18''s companion-doc mandate nor §11.4.44''s revision header is enforced by any invariant.\u000a\u000aTHE PERVERSE CONSEQUENCE, MEASURED: a new script with NO companion doc passes the gate. Writing the companion doc that §11.4.18 MANDATES creates docs/scripts/<name>.md, which invariant 16 (CM-MARKDOWN-EXPORT-SYNC) then requires to have .html and .pdf twins — and their absence is a BLOCKING failure. This session hit it exactly: docs/scripts/test_gitignore_swallow_is_loud.{html,pdf} are missing and are two of invariant 16''s six violations.\u000aSo the gate''s incentive gradient points AWAY from the constitution: complying with §11.4.18 is punished, ignoring it is free. That is worse than an ungated rule — it is a rule the machinery actively discourages.\u000a\u000a§11.4.227 IS THE GOVERNING ANCHOR: a named gate that exists only in prose is gate debt, and the ledger of unimplemented CM-* names must be monotone-decreasing. CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is named in §11.4.18''s own text and implemented nowhere — one concrete row of exactly the 58%-unimplemented population §11.4.227 was minted to shrink.\u000a\u000aACCEPTANCE: (1) either CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is implemented, or it is registered as a deferral pointing at a tracked §11.4.197 item — silent absence is what §11.4.227 forbids; (2) same for §11.4.44''s header check; (3) whichever is chosen, the incentive inversion is closed: it must never be cheaper to skip a mandated doc than to write one — if invariant 16 will demand twins, the doc-creation path must produce them, or invariant 16 must scope out docs/scripts until it can; (4) a paired §1.1 mutation per gate implemented.\u000a\u000aHONEST NOTE ON SCOPE: this item does not argue §11.4.18 should be enforced immediately — that is an operator call about gate debt priority (§11.4.66). It argues the CURRENT state is incoherent: an unenforced mandate whose observance triggers a different gate''s failure. Either enforce both ends or neither.\u000a\u000aDISCOVERY CHANNEL (§11.4.238): found by the T042 readiness preflight while explaining why a new file broke invariant 16. Not by the automated QA regime.'),NULL,NULL,NULL,'','','Fixed',unistr('## BOB-223 — §11.4.18 script-documentation and §11.4.44 revision headers are ungated — and the perverse consequence is that WRITING the mandated companion doc is what breaks the build\u000a\u000a**Status:** Fixed (→ Fixed.md)\u000a**Type:** Bug\u000a**Evidence:** docs/qa/BOB-223/closure_evidence_20260925.md\u000a**Severity:** major\u000a\u000aWHAT, both conductor-verified with control needles: CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC occurrences in scripts/pre_build_verification.sh = 0 (control needle CM-MARKDOWN-EXPORT-SYNC = 6, so the instrument sees). §11.4.44 revision-header enforcement likewise 0 hits (control needle 3). Neither §11.4.18''s companion-doc mandate nor §11.4.44''s revision header is enforced by any invariant.\u000a\u000aTHE PERVERSE CONSEQUENCE, MEASURED: a new script with NO companion doc passes the gate. Writing the companion doc that §11.4.18 MANDATES creates docs/scripts/<name>.md, which invariant 16 (CM-MARKDOWN-EXPORT-SYNC) then requires to have .html and .pdf twins — and their absence is a BLOCKING failure. This session hit it exactly: docs/scripts/test_gitignore_swallow_is_loud.{html,pdf} are missing and are two of invariant 16''s six violations.\u000aSo the gate''s incentive gradient points AWAY from the constitution: complying with §11.4.18 is punished, ignoring it is free. That is worse than an ungated rule — it is a rule the machinery actively discourages.\u000a\u000a§11.4.227 IS THE GOVERNING ANCHOR: a named gate that exists only in prose is gate debt, and the ledger of unimplemented CM-* names must be monotone-decreasing. CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is named in §11.4.18''s own text and implemented nowhere — one concrete row of exactly the 58%-unimplemented population §11.4.227 was minted to shrink.\u000a\u000aACCEPTANCE: (1) either CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is implemented, or it is registered as a deferral pointing at a tracked §11.4.197 item — silent absence is what §11.4.227 forbids; (2) same for §11.4.44''s header check; (3) whichever is chosen, the incentive inversion is closed: it must never be cheaper to skip a mandated doc than to write one — if invariant 16 will demand twins, the doc-creation path must produce them, or invariant 16 must scope out docs/scripts until it can; (4) a paired §1.1 mutation per gate implemented.\u000a\u000aHONEST NOTE ON SCOPE: this item does not argue §11.4.18 should be enforced immediately — that is an operator call about gate debt priority (§11.4.66). It argues the CURRENT state is incoherent: an unenforced mandate whose observance triggers a different gate''s failure. Either enforce both ends or neither.\u000a\u000aDISCOVERY CHANNEL (§11.4.238): found by the T042 readiness preflight while explaining why a new file broke invariant 16. Not by the automated QA regime.\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 12:40:53','2026-09-25 12:40:53',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-151','Task','Obsolete (→ Fixed.md)','Medium','CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is a named gate with no implementation, and 24 of 36 scripts have no companion doc','CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is a named gate with no implementation, and 24 of 36 scripts have no companion doc',NULL,NULL,NULL,'AI','','Fixed',unistr('## BOB-151 — CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is a named gate with no implementation, and 24 of 36 scripts have no companion doc\u000a\u000a**Status:** Obsolete (→ Fixed.md)\u000a**Type:** Task\u000a**Evidence:** docs/qa/BOB-223/closure_evidence_20260925.md\u000a**Severity:** Medium\u000a**Created-By:** AI\u000a**Obsolete-Details:** Since: 2026-09-25; Reason: duplicate-of; Superseding-item: BOB-223; Triple-check evidence: docs/qa/BOB-223/closure_evidence_20260925.md\u000a\u000aCM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC is a named gate with no implementation, and 24 of 36 scripts have no companion doc\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 12:40:53','2026-09-25 12:41:08',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-242','Task','Queued',NULL,'Implement CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC (§11.4.18) and CM-DOC-REVISION-HEADER-PRESENT (§11.4.44) -- the two gates BOB-223 found named-but-unimplemented and registered as deferrals','BOB-223 closed the incentive inversion where writing a §11.4.18-mandated docs/scripts/<name>.md companion doc tripped invariant 16 while the mandate requiring the doc to exist (CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC) has zero implementation, and the doc''s required §11.4.44 revision header (CM-DOC-REVISION-HEADER-PRESENT) is likewise unenforced outside one unrelated ledger file. Both are now registered as explicit GATE-DEBT REGISTER deferrals in scripts/pre_build_verification.sh, satisfying §11.4.227(A)''s bar for now, but the underlying mandates remain unenforced. This item implements BOTH: (1) walk every *.sh/*.bash under scripts/, require a docs/scripts/<name>.md companion (24 of 36 currently lack one per BOB-151''s own count), verify same-commit-or-newer mtime per §11.4.18''s literal text; (2) require every in-scope companion doc to carry **Revision:**/**Last modified:** per §11.4.44. Both need an operator brownfield-adoption decision (§11.4.224(E)/§11.4.66 -- immediate hard floor vs. monotone-decrease ratchet vs. changed-files-only), a paired §1.1 mutation each, and -- once landed -- removal of both DEFERRED: lines from the GATE-DEBT REGISTER in scripts/pre_build_verification.sh. Duplicate-of/originating-from: BOB-223, BOB-151. Also recommend adding two rows to constitution/scripts/gates/gate_ledger_deferrals.tsv (the constitution submodule''s own canonical §11.4.227(A) deferral ledger) once this new item''s ID is known.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Claude','Claude','Issues',unistr('## BOB-242 — Implement CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC (§11.4.18) and CM-DOC-REVISION-HEADER-PRESENT (§11.4.44) -- the two gates BOB-223 found named-but-unimplemented and registered as deferrals\u000a\u000a**Status:** Queued\u000a**Type:** Task\u000a**Created-By:** Claude\u000a**Assigned-To:** Claude\u000a\u000aBOB-223 closed the incentive inversion where writing a §11.4.18-mandated docs/scripts/<name>.md companion doc tripped invariant 16 while the mandate requiring the doc to exist (CM-SCRIPT-DOCS-SYNC) has zero implementation, and the doc''s required §11.4.44 revision header (CM-DOC-REVISION-HEADER-PRESENT) is likewise unenforced outside one unrelated ledger file. Both are now registered as explicit GATE-DEBT REGISTER deferrals in scripts/pre_build_verification.sh, satisfying §11.4.227(A)''s bar for now, but the underlying mandates remain unenforced. This item implements BOTH: (1) walk every *.sh/*.bash under scripts/, require a docs/scripts/<name>.md companion (24 of 36 currently lack one per BOB-151''s own count), verify same-commit-or-newer mtime per §11.4.18''s literal text; (2) require every in-scope companion doc to carry **Revision:**/**Last modified:** per §11.4.44. Both need an operator brownfield-adoption decision (§11.4.224(E)/§11.4.66 -- immediate hard floor vs. monotone-decrease ratchet vs. changed-files-only), a paired §1.1 mutation each, and -- once landed -- removal of both DEFERRED: lines from the GATE-DEBT REGISTER in scripts/pre_build_verification.sh. Duplicate-of/originating-from: BOB-223, BOB-151. Also recommend adding two rows to constitution/scripts/gates/gate_ledger_deferrals.tsv (the constitution submodule''s own canonical §11.4.227(A) deferral ledger) once this new item''s ID is known.\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 12:41:24','2026-09-25 12:41:24',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-243','Bug','Queued',NULL,'CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD: 4 first-party source files under .specify/extensions/superspec/ silently swallowed by .gitignore','Discovered by a full 58-invariant pre_build_verification.sh sweep (2026-09-25) run during BOB-223 closure verification: invariant 56 (CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD, §11.4.201(6), BOB-212) reports 4 first-party source files silently ignored: .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/e2e-agent-claude.sh, .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/e2e-smoke.sh, .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/validate-extension-metadata.py, .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/validate-release-archive.py -- all blocked by the broad .gitignore:218 rule ''.specify/extensions/superspec/''. Unrelated to BOB-223''s own scope; a genuinely new finding, not previously tracked. Remedy per the gate''s own remediation text: either rename/relocate the files so no .gitignore rule matches them, or add an explicit ! negation for them in .gitignore, then re-run the guard. Investigate first per §11.4.6/§11.4.124 whether the broad .specify/extensions/superspec/ ignore rule was intentional (e.g. to exclude a vendored/generated subtree) before narrowing it, since a careless negation could re-expose something the rule was deliberately protecting.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Claude','Claude','Issues',unistr('## BOB-243 — CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD: 4 first-party source files under .specify/extensions/superspec/ silently swallowed by .gitignore\u000a\u000a**Status:** Queued\u000a**Type:** Bug\u000a**Created-By:** Claude\u000a**Assigned-To:** Claude\u000a\u000aDiscovered by a full 58-invariant pre_build_verification.sh sweep (2026-09-25) run during BOB-223 closure verification: invariant 56 (CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD, §11.4.201(6), BOB-212) reports 4 first-party source files silently ignored: .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/e2e-agent-claude.sh, .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/e2e-smoke.sh, .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/validate-extension-metadata.py, .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/validate-release-archive.py -- all blocked by the broad .gitignore:218 rule ''.specify/extensions/superspec/''. Unrelated to BOB-223''s own scope; a genuinely new finding, not previously tracked. Remedy per the gate''s own remediation text: either rename/relocate the files so no .gitignore rule matches them, or add an explicit ! negation for them in .gitignore, then re-run the guard. Investigate first per §11.4.6/§11.4.124 whether the broad .specify/extensions/superspec/ ignore rule was intentional (e.g. to exclude a vendored/generated subtree) before narrowing it, since a careless negation could re-expose something the rule was deliberately protecting.\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 12:41:24','2026-09-25 12:41:24',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-240','Task','Completed (→ Fixed.md)','medium','workable-items close/update do not validate the status word against the item''s Type (§11.4.33) — extend CLI + validate invariant (BOB-239 mechanical-fix half)',unistr('WHAT: split from BOB-239 (closed 2026-09-25 after bulk-correcting 30\u000apre-existing §11.4.33 closure-vocabulary violations). This item is the\u000aremaining MECHANICAL-PREVENTION half: extend\u000aconstitution/scripts/workable-items'' `close` and `update` subcommands to\u000aVALIDATE the chosen status word against the item''s own Type (Bug->Fixed,\u000aFeature->Implemented, Task->Completed, any type->Obsolete) and REFUSE a\u000amismatched call rather than silently accepting it. Also extend the\u000a`validate` subcommand''s existing invariant set to catch this class for\u000adefense-in-depth — confirmed this session that `validate: OK` ran\u000arepeatedly against a DB simultaneously holding 30+ live violations of\u000athis exact class, so the current invariant set does not check it.\u000a\u000aEVIDENCE THIS IS A REAL, RECURRING MISTAKE, NOT A HYPOTHETICAL: this\u000asession''s own conductor made the identical error 4 times in a row\u000a(BOB-077/100/179/226, all Type=Task closed with `--status fixed`) before\u000aan unrelated self-audit caught it — on a DB that ALREADY held 30\u000ahistorical instances of the same mistake from earlier sessions. A\u000aCLI-level guard would have refused every one of those 34 calls at the\u000amoment they were made, instead of requiring a human/agent to remember to\u000aaudit for it afterward.\u000a\u000aSCOPE: constitution/scripts/workable-items/ (Go source) — a UNIVERSAL,\u000aconstitution-submodule-owned tool, per §11.4.17. Landing a real fix here\u000aneeds the §11.4.26 fetch/merge/push-to-all-upstreams workflow, same as\u000aBOB-191''s gate fix this session, NOT boba''s own commit-push-all.sh.\u000a\u000aACCEPTANCE: (1) `workable-items close --status <word>` refuses when\u000a<word>''s implied Type-mapping does not match the target item''s actual\u000aType, printing the correct word to use; (2) same for `update --status`;\u000a(3) `validate` gains a new invariant scanning every Fixed-location item\u000afor a Type/Status mismatch per the closed §11.4.33 mapping, FAILing (not\u000asilently passing) on any hit; (4) each of (1)-(3) ships a paired §1.1\u000amutation proving the check is load-bearing (a neutered version of the\u000acheck must let a known-bad Type/Status pair through); (5) the Obsolete\u000astatus is correctly treated as valid for ANY Type (it is not part of the\u000atype-specific mapping) so the new check does not false-positive on\u000alegitimately Obsolete-closed items.\u000a\u000aDISCOVERY CHANNEL (§11.4.238): found by the conductor''s own repeated,\u000aself-caught instances of the mistake this session, generalised into\u000aBOB-239 (the bulk-correction), now split into this item (the mechanical\u000aprevention) per BOB-239''s own acceptance criterion 2/3.'),NULL,NULL,NULL,'AI','AI','Fixed',unistr('## BOB-240 — workable-items close/update do not validate the status word against the item''s Type (§11.4.33) — extend CLI + validate invariant (BOB-239 mechanical-fix half)\u000a\u000a**Status:** Completed (→ Fixed.md)\u000a**Type:** Task\u000a**Evidence:** docs/qa/BOB-240/closure_evidence_20260925.md\u000a**Severity:** medium\u000a**Created-By:** AI\u000a**Assigned-To:** AI\u000a\u000aWHAT: split from BOB-239 (closed 2026-09-25 after bulk-correcting 30\u000apre-existing §11.4.33 closure-vocabulary violations). This item is the\u000aremaining MECHANICAL-PREVENTION half: extend\u000aconstitution/scripts/workable-items'' `close` and `update` subcommands to\u000aVALIDATE the chosen status word against the item''s own Type (Bug->Fixed,\u000aFeature->Implemented, Task->Completed, any type->Obsolete) and REFUSE a\u000amismatched call rather than silently accepting it. Also extend the\u000a`validate` subcommand''s existing invariant set to catch this class for\u000adefense-in-depth — confirmed this session that `validate: OK` ran\u000arepeatedly against a DB simultaneously holding 30+ live violations of\u000athis exact class, so the current invariant set does not check it.\u000a\u000aEVIDENCE THIS IS A REAL, RECURRING MISTAKE, NOT A HYPOTHETICAL: this\u000asession''s own conductor made the identical error 4 times in a row\u000a(BOB-077/100/179/226, all Type=Task closed with `--status fixed`) before\u000aan unrelated self-audit caught it — on a DB that ALREADY held 30\u000ahistorical instances of the same mistake from earlier sessions. A\u000aCLI-level guard would have refused every one of those 34 calls at the\u000amoment they were made, instead of requiring a human/agent to remember to\u000aaudit for it afterward.\u000a\u000aSCOPE: constitution/scripts/workable-items/ (Go source) — a UNIVERSAL,\u000aconstitution-submodule-owned tool, per §11.4.17. Landing a real fix here\u000aneeds the §11.4.26 fetch/merge/push-to-all-upstreams workflow, same as\u000aBOB-191''s gate fix this session, NOT boba''s own commit-push-all.sh.\u000a\u000aACCEPTANCE: (1) `workable-items close --status <word>` refuses when\u000a<word>''s implied Type-mapping does not match the target item''s actual\u000aType, printing the correct word to use; (2) same for `update --status`;\u000a(3) `validate` gains a new invariant scanning every Fixed-location item\u000afor a Type/Status mismatch per the closed §11.4.33 mapping, FAILing (not\u000asilently passing) on any hit; (4) each of (1)-(3) ships a paired §1.1\u000amutation proving the check is load-bearing (a neutered version of the\u000acheck must let a known-bad Type/Status pair through); (5) the Obsolete\u000astatus is correctly treated as valid for ANY Type (it is not part of the\u000atype-specific mapping) so the new check does not false-positive on\u000alegitimately Obsolete-closed items.\u000a\u000aDISCOVERY CHANNEL (§11.4.238): found by the conductor''s own repeated,\u000aself-caught instances of the mistake this session, generalised into\u000aBOB-239 (the bulk-correction), now split into this item (the mechanical\u000aprevention) per BOB-239''s own acceptance criterion 2/3.\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 14:07:28','2026-09-25 14:07:28',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-244','Bug','Queued','Critical','CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD: 4 first-party superspec scripts silently swallowed by .gitignore:218','Discovered 2026-09-25 by the pre-build sweep''s own CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD gate (§11.4.201(6), BOB-212 pattern), during the 003-zero-shortcomings-audit feature''s setup phase. What: 4 genuine first-party files under .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/ — e2e-agent-claude.sh (19458 bytes), e2e-smoke.sh (8757 bytes), validate-extension-metadata.py (5888 bytes), validate-release-archive.py (7053 bytes), all dated Aug 31 2026 — are untracked by git (confirmed via ''git ls-files --error-unmatch'': did not match any file(s) known to git) and are BLOCKED from ever being staged by the broad directory-level ignore rule at .gitignore:218 (.specify/extensions/superspec/). Root cause investigation needed: .gitignore:218''s own comment states the WHOLE directory is ignored because it is ''the vendored superspec extension checkout'' that ''carries its OWN .git (gitdir pointer)... and DUPLICATES the root superspec submodule'' — but these 4 specific files look like genuine first-party CI/e2e/validation tooling, not vendored upstream content, and predate today''s session (Aug 31 mtime). Per §11.4.124 (investigate-before-remove) and §11.4.122 (no silent removal without operator decision), this needs git-history investigation (was there ever a commit touching these paths? are they meant to ship with this project or are they truly part of the vendored nested checkout and should stay ignored?) before either (a) carving a negation exception into .gitignore for exactly these 4 files, or (b) confirming they are genuinely disposable vendored artifacts and documenting that explicitly. Acceptance: CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD passes clean (0 findings) OR the 4 files are explicitly, evidence-backed classified as vendored-and-correctly-ignored with that classification recorded in the .gitignore comment itself.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'AI','AI','Issues',unistr('## BOB-244 — CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD: 4 first-party superspec scripts silently swallowed by .gitignore:218\u000a\u000a**Status:** Queued\u000a**Type:** Bug\u000a**Severity:** Critical\u000a**Created-By:** AI\u000a**Assigned-To:** AI\u000a\u000aDiscovered 2026-09-25 by the pre-build sweep''s own CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD gate (§11.4.201(6), BOB-212 pattern), during the 003-zero-shortcomings-audit feature''s setup phase. What: 4 genuine first-party files under .specify/extensions/superspec/scripts/ — e2e-agent-claude.sh (19458 bytes), e2e-smoke.sh (8757 bytes), validate-extension-metadata.py (5888 bytes), validate-release-archive.py (7053 bytes), all dated Aug 31 2026 — are untracked by git (confirmed via ''git ls-files --error-unmatch'': did not match any file(s) known to git) and are BLOCKED from ever being staged by the broad directory-level ignore rule at .gitignore:218 (.specify/extensions/superspec/). Root cause investigation needed: .gitignore:218''s own comment states the WHOLE directory is ignored because it is ''the vendored superspec extension checkout'' that ''carries its OWN .git (gitdir pointer)... and DUPLICATES the root superspec submodule'' — but these 4 specific files look like genuine first-party CI/e2e/validation tooling, not vendored upstream content, and predate today''s session (Aug 31 mtime). Per §11.4.124 (investigate-before-remove) and §11.4.122 (no silent removal without operator decision), this needs git-history investigation (was there ever a commit touching these paths? are they meant to ship with this project or are they truly part of the vendored nested checkout and should stay ignored?) before either (a) carving a negation exception into .gitignore for exactly these 4 files, or (b) confirming they are genuinely disposable vendored artifacts and documenting that explicitly. Acceptance: CM-GITIGNORE-SWALLOW-GUARD passes clean (0 findings) OR the 4 files are explicitly, evidence-backed classified as vendored-and-correctly-ignored with that classification recorded in the .gitignore comment itself.\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 14:28:46','2026-09-25 14:28:46',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
+INSERT INTO items VALUES('BOB-245','Bug','Fixed (→ Fixed.md)','Medium','git pre-commit mutation-marker guard false-positive-blocks legitimate docs/test prose describing the §1.1 methodology','scripts/git_hooks/pre-commit (tracked source; installed to .git/hooks/pre-commit by scripts/install_git_hooks.sh) did a naive, unscoped grep for the literal string MUTATED (and two sibling markers) across EVERY staged file, with zero ability to distinguish a genuine leftover mutation-test artifact in shipped production code from legitimate prose in docs/QA-evidence files or legitimate comments in test sources that correctly and intentionally describe this project''s own MANDATORY paired §1.1 mutation-testing methodology (e.g. the standard phrasing GREEN on the UNMUTATED sandbox copy, RED on the MUTATED sandbox copy). Confirmed real false-positive instances that blocked an otherwise-clean commit this session: docs/qa/BOB-187/closure_evidence_20260925.md line 83 (+ .html twin line 271) - prose describing an UNMUTATED sandbox reproduction; docs/qa/BOB-196/closure_evidence_20260925.md line 232 (+ .html twin line 461) - a documented shell variable name MUTATED_RC=1 inside a code-fence describing a reproduction script; tests/unit/test_ownership_precondition.sh lines 642 and 677 - comments GREEN on the UNMUTATED sandbox copy / RED on the MUTATED sandbox copy, a FRESH escape target. FIX: adopted the same scope-restriction technique already proven in the sibling gate scripts/pre_build/check_cm_no_production_mutation_residue.sh - the hook now filters the staged-file list to only first-party PRODUCTION source roots (download-proxy, qBitTorrent-go, scripts, plugins, webui-bridge.py) of a scannable type (.sh/.bash/.py/.go), explicitly excluding tests/, docs/, qa-results/, scratchpad/, constitution/, submodules/, challenges/, mutants/, and vendored/build-output directories, via new _pc_is_excluded_path / _pc_is_scannable_type / _pc_is_production_path helper functions. Self-avoidance (string-concatenated marker tokens, and this hook''s own new comments avoiding literal marker spelling) preserved. No fenced waiver escape was added (judged unnecessary for this simpler hook; documented in-source why, with a pointer to the sibling gate''s guardrails:allow mechanism as the extension point if ever needed). TESTS: new hermetic test tests/hooks/test_pre_commit_mutation_scope.sh drives the real invocation path against a throwaway mktemp -d git repo (never the real project repo) - Test 1/1b prove the RED-then-GREEN fix (legitimate marker-containing prose under docs/ and tests/ now exits 0), Test 2 is a negative control proving a genuine residue-shaped marker staged under scripts/ (a production root) still exits 1 and names the offending file, Test 3 proves a clean file still exits 0. All 7 assertions PASS. A paired §1.1 mutation (commenting out the _pc_is_production_path scope-gate call, restoring pre-fix unscoped behaviour) was manually applied and confirmed to flip Tests 1 and 1b to FAIL (5 passed, 2 failed), then the mutation was reverted and GREEN (7/7) was re-confirmed - proving the test genuinely catches a regression to the pre-fix behaviour. VERIFICATION: reinstalled the fixed hook via scripts/install_git_hooks.sh, staged the original 5 flagged files, ran the installed .git/hooks/pre-commit directly, confirmed exit 0 with no false-positive output, then git restore --staged those 5 files (they belong to separate, already-in-flight work and were not committed by this fix).',NULL,NULL,NULL,'AI','AI','Fixed',unistr('## BOB-245 — git pre-commit mutation-marker guard false-positive-blocks legitimate docs/test prose describing the §1.1 methodology\u000a\u000a**Status:** Fixed (→ Fixed.md)\u000a**Type:** Bug\u000a**Evidence:** docs/qa/BOB-245/closure_evidence_20260925.md\u000a**Severity:** Medium\u000a**Created-By:** AI\u000a**Assigned-To:** AI\u000a\u000ascripts/git_hooks/pre-commit (tracked source; installed to .git/hooks/pre-commit by scripts/install_git_hooks.sh) did a naive, unscoped grep for the literal string MUTATED (and two sibling markers) across EVERY staged file, with zero ability to distinguish a genuine leftover mutation-test artifact in shipped production code from legitimate prose in docs/QA-evidence files or legitimate comments in test sources that correctly and intentionally describe this project''s own MANDATORY paired §1.1 mutation-testing methodology (e.g. the standard phrasing GREEN on the UNMUTATED sandbox copy, RED on the MUTATED sandbox copy). Confirmed real false-positive instances that blocked an otherwise-clean commit this session: docs/qa/BOB-187/closure_evidence_20260925.md line 83 (+ .html twin line 271) - prose describing an UNMUTATED sandbox reproduction; docs/qa/BOB-196/closure_evidence_20260925.md line 232 (+ .html twin line 461) - a documented shell variable name MUTATED_RC=1 inside a code-fence describing a reproduction script; tests/unit/test_ownership_precondition.sh lines 642 and 677 - comments GREEN on the UNMUTATED sandbox copy / RED on the MUTATED sandbox copy, a FRESH escape target. FIX: adopted the same scope-restriction technique already proven in the sibling gate scripts/pre_build/check_cm_no_production_mutation_residue.sh - the hook now filters the staged-file list to only first-party PRODUCTION source roots (download-proxy, qBitTorrent-go, scripts, plugins, webui-bridge.py) of a scannable type (.sh/.bash/.py/.go), explicitly excluding tests/, docs/, qa-results/, scratchpad/, constitution/, submodules/, challenges/, mutants/, and vendored/build-output directories, via new _pc_is_excluded_path / _pc_is_scannable_type / _pc_is_production_path helper functions. Self-avoidance (string-concatenated marker tokens, and this hook''s own new comments avoiding literal marker spelling) preserved. No fenced waiver escape was added (judged unnecessary for this simpler hook; documented in-source why, with a pointer to the sibling gate''s guardrails:allow mechanism as the extension point if ever needed). TESTS: new hermetic test tests/hooks/test_pre_commit_mutation_scope.sh drives the real invocation path against a throwaway mktemp -d git repo (never the real project repo) - Test 1/1b prove the RED-then-GREEN fix (legitimate marker-containing prose under docs/ and tests/ now exits 0), Test 2 is a negative control proving a genuine residue-shaped marker staged under scripts/ (a production root) still exits 1 and names the offending file, Test 3 proves a clean file still exits 0. All 7 assertions PASS. A paired §1.1 mutation (commenting out the _pc_is_production_path scope-gate call, restoring pre-fix unscoped behaviour) was manually applied and confirmed to flip Tests 1 and 1b to FAIL (5 passed, 2 failed), then the mutation was reverted and GREEN (7/7) was re-confirmed - proving the test genuinely catches a regression to the pre-fix behaviour. VERIFICATION: reinstalled the fixed hook via scripts/install_git_hooks.sh, staged the original 5 flagged files, ran the installed .git/hooks/pre-commit directly, confirmed exit 0 with no false-positive output, then git restore --staged those 5 files (they belong to separate, already-in-flight work and were not committed by this fix).\u000a\u000a'),'section',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-25 14:49:36','2026-09-25 14:49:36',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL);
